      "text": "1,406,712,094.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 607069464 and 799642630?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Align the numbers by their place values:**\n\n```\n  607,069,464\n+ 799,642,630\n```\n\n2. **Add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left:**\n\n```\n     6 0 7 0 6 9 4 6 4\n   + 7 9 9 6 4 2 6 3 0\n   -----------------------\n     1 4 0 6 7 1 2 0 9 4\n```\n\n3. **Carry over any excess value to the next higher place value if the sum exceeds 9:**\n\n- **Ones place:** 4 + 0 = 4\n- **Tens place:** 6 + 3 = 9\n- **Hundreds place:** 4 + 6 = 10 (Write down 0 and carry over 1)\n- **Thousands place:** 9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 (Write down 2 and carry over 1)\n- **Ten-thousands place:** 6 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 11 (Write down 1 and carry over 1)\n- **Hundred-thousands place:** 0 + 6 + 1 (carry) = 7\n- **Millions place:** 7 + 9 = 16 (Write down 6 and carry over 1)\n- **Ten-millions place:** 0 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 10 (Write down 0 and carry over 1)\n- **Hundred-millions place:** 6 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 14 (Write down 4 and carry over 1)\n- **Billions place:** 0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 1\n\n4. **Combine all the results to get the final sum:**\n\n```\n1,406,712,094\n```\n\n# Answer:\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\boxed{1406712094}.",
